==German==
===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|De-at-abfahren.ogg|audio (Austria)}}
*{{IPA|[ˈapfaːrən]}}

===Etymology===
Compound of ''[[ab]]'' (‘from’) and ''[[fahren]]'' (‘drive’).

===Verb===
'''abfahren''' (''third-person singular simple present'' '''[[fährt ab]]''', ''[[past tense]]'' '''[[fuhr ab]]''', ''[[past participle]]'' '''[[abgefahren]] sein''')

# to [[depart]], to [[leave]]
#* ''[[Ihr|Ihr]] [[Zug]] '''fährt''' [[um]] [[fünf]] [[Uhr]] '''ab.''''' 
#*: His train departs at 5 o'clock.
#* ''[[wir|Wir]] [[werden]] [[morgen]] '''abfahren.'''
#*: We will leave tomorrow
# {{colloquial|lang=de}} to be crazy about something.
#* ''[[sie|Sie]] '''fährt''' [[voll]] [[auf]] [[Kultfilm]]e '''ab.'''''
#*: She's really crazy about cult movies.

====Synonyms====
*[[abreisen]]
*auf etw. [[stehen]]

====Derived terms====
*[[Abfahrt]] (departure; ski-run)

